meta {
  name: Space Notify Credential Revoked
  type: http
  seq: 167
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.notifyCredentialRevoked
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{serviceAuthToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main",
    "credentials": ["3l2kq7xzv5b2a"]
  }
}

docs {
  A space authority telling this repo host that space credentials it issued are revoked, by jti
  (1–100 per call). From then on any read presenting one of those credentials is refused 401, until
  the revocation lapses an hour and a few seconds later — past the longest life a credential can
  have. Short credential lifetime remains the main revocation mechanism; this is the fast path.

  Authenticated with service auth (Authorization: Bearer <service-auth JWT>, lxm =
  com.atproto.space.notifyCredentialRevoked). The issuer must be the space's authority; its key is
  resolved from the network, so it need not be a local account. aud is a repo DID hosted here (as
  the lexicon describes) or this server's own DID; anything else is 401.

  Idempotent. A revocation for a space this server holds nothing of is accepted and dropped.
}
